        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_api_key.py** - Fetches an API key from Azure Key Vault.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_db_secret.py** - Fetches a database connection secret from Azure Key Vault.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] parse_json_secret.py** - Retrieves and parses a JSON-formatted secret from Azure Key Vault.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] rotate_secret_version.py** - Reads a specific secret version from Azure Key Vault.\n5. **[HELPER] security_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Azure Key Vault.\n6. **[HELPER] security_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Azure Key Vault.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] rotation_summary.py** - Placeholder for summarizing secret rotation status.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] secret_label_safety.py** - Placeholder for checking secret labels and notes for unsafe text.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] secret_audit_embedding.py** - Placeholder for embedding secret audit notes for semantic search.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] runbook_translate.py** - Placeholder for translating secret-rotation runbook notes.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Azure Key Vault as the concrete external provider, making it identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities. The later-step scored files are placeholders for future implementations.",
